<!-- INTRODUCTION -->
<section class="acdt-intro content-section" aria-labelledby="intro-heading">
  <h2 id="intro-heading" class="sr-only">About Alaska Daylight Time to Eastern Standard Time Conversion</h2>
  <p>
    Welcome to our dedicated <strong>AKDT to EST Converter</strong>, designed for aviation dispatchers, petroleum engineers, seafood logistics coordinators, and domestic travelers managing schedules across Alaska Daylight Time (UTC-8) and Eastern Standard Time (UTC-5). AKDT represents the summer daylight saving time zone for Alaska.
  </p>
  <p>
    Operating 3 hours behind US Eastern Standard Time, Alaska occupies a vital geographic position for transpacific air cargo logistics, maritime fisheries, and national energy production. Ted Stevens Anchorage International Airport serves as a global air cargo crossroads connecting North America, Asia, and Europe.
  </p>
  <p>
    Eastern Standard Time (EST) governs commerce across the US East Coast in winter (including New York, Toronto, Miami, and Washington D.C.). Coordinating business operations between Anchorage and New York offers an advantageous 6-hour shared business window.
  </p>
  <p>
    Explore our interactive live clocks, dynamic conversion tool, 24-hour reference matrix, domestic meeting planner recommendations, and technical timezone database specifications below.
