      <text x="600" y="147" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#36c7b5">07:00 PM</text>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>1. The +3 Addition Formula</h3>
      <p>Add 3 hours to the Alaska time. For example, 08:00 AM AKDT + 3 hours = 11:00 AM EST. If the total exceeds 24:00, roll over into the next day.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>2. Shared Domestic US Overlap</h3>
      <p>With only a 3-hour gap, Alaskan and East Coast offices enjoy a 6-hour daily overlap from 8:00 AM to 2:00 PM AKDT (11:00 AM to 5:00 PM EST).</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>3. Summer Synchronized Shifts</h3>
      <p>When North America enters summer daylight saving, Alaska moves to AKDT (UTC-8) and Eastern US moves to EDT (UTC-4), maintaining a 4-hour gap during summer.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>4. Transpacific Air Cargo Alignment</h3>
      <p>Air cargo couriers in Anchorage align flight departure logs with East Coast distribution hubs in New York and Atlanta using real-time AKDT/EST conversions.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- STEP BY STEP GUIDE -->
<section class="content-section" id="step-by-step-guide" aria-labelledby="step-heading">
