      <p>Identify your starting Alaska Daylight Time (UTC-8) value.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Step 2: Add 3 Hours for EST</h3>
      <p>Perform the simple mathematical addition of 3 hours. For example, 13:00 AKDT becomes 16:00 EST in New York.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Step 3: Check Next-Day Boundary Shift</h3>
      <p>If AKDT time is 10:00 PM or 11:00 PM, adding 3 hours shifts the local EST timestamp past midnight into the next morning.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Step 4: Verify Target US Region</h3>
      <p>Confirm that your East Coast contact is operating under Eastern Standard Time (America/New_York).</p>
    </article>
